WEBVTT

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:04.520
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.520
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.020
The sun is shining brightly, isn't it?

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.530
If we leave them like this, 
the zabutons will get nice and fluffy.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.080
Yes, they will.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.360
I'm going now!

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.790
Be careful!

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:16.920
I'm going now!

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:19.560
Where is she going?

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:21.200
The library.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.040
Oh, yeah. Yesterday she was writing 
a book report, wasn't she?

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:29.450
Very different from you wailing on the 
last day of summer vacation, isn't it?

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:32.640
Now, you're in the way. Step aside.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.200
I have a lot to get ready, you know?

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.470
"Get ready"?

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:45.900
<b>Recipe for
 Happiness</b>

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:13.770
<b>Welcoming the Spirits</b>

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.370
<i>Wow...</i>

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:26.620
<i>They have quite a few books about wagashi here.</i>

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:28.330
Mitsuru-chan!

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:30.280
I-Itsuka-chan?

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:31.980
Are you looking for something?

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:36.640
Oh, no! I was just thinking maybe I could 
make some snacks for my little brothers.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.470
Wagashi? In that case, why don't you 
try asking everyone at Ryokushou?

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:41.770
What? Ask Nagomu-san?!

00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:43.760
It's not limited just to him.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.380
Shh.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:48.300
Thank you for all your work today!

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:49.270
<b>Kafuuen</b>

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.770
<i>Well, now... What should I do for lunch?</i>

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:56.330
Are you sure you didn't 
want to borrow any books?

00:02:56.330 --> 00:03:00.150
Yes. I thought I'd ask for their 
requests and then go back.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:05.910
<i>I got to leave work early, so maybe I'll 
stretch my legs and go somewhere lively.</i>

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:08.600
You're not helping at the shop today?

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.600
That's right! They said to go have fun.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:12.670
Yay! Then, today we should—

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:14.750
Itsuka-chan!

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:15.960
Kanoko-san!

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:18.760
You startled me. You're not in the shop today?

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:21.220
I got a day off. What about you, Kanoko-san?

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:26.500
The manager and the others have a tea party 
this afternoon, so I asked to leave early.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.100
Oh, is this your friend?

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:32.880
N-Nice to meet you. 
My name is Horikawa Mitsuru.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.610
I work part-time at Ryokushou.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:38.530
Oh, that's right! I didn't recognize 
you in your regular clothes.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:43.720
I've seen you a few times, too. 
I heard that you're a friend of Nagomu-san's.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:45.550
That's right, his friend.

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:48.160
I'm Matsukaze Kanoko. Nice to meet you.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.760
Are you two headed somewhere?

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:56.400
To have lunch at a nearby soba restaurant.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.340
Oh, that sounds good! Can I come with you?

00:03:59.340 --> 00:03:59.920
Please do!

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:03.050
Thank you! I was wondering 
what restaurant to go to.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.550
<b>Marutome</b>

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.550
<b>Soba
Restaurant</b>

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:06.550
Still...

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.270
Having soba is a little old-fashioned 
for us young people, isn't it?

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:12.410
Actually, we were just talking about wagashi,

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:16.110
so we both started craving warabi mochi.

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.380
Oh, I see.

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:21.940
<b>Lunch Set  800 yen</b>

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:21.940
<b>Zarusoba (choice of soba or udon)</b>

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:21.940
<b>Dessert included</b>

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:21.940
<b>For +500 yen, add tempura</b>

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:21.940
<b>Choice of Dessert:
 Warabi mochi
 Ice cream (Vanilla / Yuzu)
 Mini Matcha Cake</b>

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:21.940
I totally understand. You have to have 
warabi mochi in the summer, right?

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:23.040
Right?

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:24.530
I think we're going to get along great!

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.900
That makes me really happy!

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.910
<i>This situation...</i>

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:31.410
<b>Crush on
 Nagomu</b>

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:31.410
<b>Nagomu's
 Ex-Girlfriend</b>

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:30.940
<i>is complicated.</i>

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:34.940
Let's see. You're both still 
on summer vacation, right?

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.550
What do you do for lunch?

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.340
I always have what they make 
for the staff at the shop.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:41.050
Then does Nagomu have that, too?

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:44.600
Yes. People go eat whenever they're free.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:47.710
But Nagomu-san is at the bottom of 
the hierarchy, so he always goes last.

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:48.680
Really...

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:51.470
But everyone only takes about 
ten minutes to eat, so...

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:53.500
Oh, well, they are really busy.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:58.060
But eating that fast... I feel like 
he'd get food stuck in his throat.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.760
W-Water...

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:02.570
But I guess he isn't that silly.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:07.070
We have bento at my place sometimes.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.850
My oldest brother has 
soccer practice, you see.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:13.370
But when we made one for him, 
the littler ones got jealous,

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:15.550
so we make them for everyone.

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:17.750
Wow, that's really sweet of you.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:21.280
Back when I was in Tokyo, I had bento, too.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.630
Making them yourself is better,

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:25.510
but thinking about what to 
make was too much work, so...

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:29.310
I understand. With the side dishes and things,
 you tend to get into a pattern, right?

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:33.390
That's right. For Nagomu especially,
 he likes kids' food.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:38.400
When I used things like chicken karaage, 
or hamburger patties, he was so happy.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.890
Since a lot of it could be frozen, 
it did make things easier, but still.

00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:44.230
You made Nagomu-san's bento for him, too?

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:47.990
Yes, but that was only 
up until six months ago.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.020
Hm?

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.490
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:53.870
<b>Menu</b>

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:56.250
I-It's here! The warabi mochi is here!

00:05:56.250 --> 00:06:00.000
L-Let's have some! You can really taste 
the wasanbon in the ones here!

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:01.750
Right, Mitsuru-chan?

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:03.750
Right.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:11.010
<b>Soba Restaurant</b>

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.610
Oh, that was delicious!

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:11.010
I think I'll go there again.

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:15.020
Mitsuru-chan, are you okay?

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.270
Why do you ask?

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:18.270
I feel like you seem a little down.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.520
You think so? I'm completely fine.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:23.070
After all, during the period 
where Kanoko-san didn't know

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:24.780
what Nagomu-san was doing, I did.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:27.270
And the same goes for you, right, Itsuka-chan?

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:34.040
Wow, you play guitar, too, 
Mitsuru-chan? You're so cool!

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.160
Kanoko-san, you don't play?

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:38.660
Country

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.660
Oh, well, I just liked to listen.

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:41.170
Is that a book you were looking for?

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:45.580
The band Nagomu-san was in 
played some country music,

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:47.170
so I started wondering about it.

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:48.740
Really?

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:55.060
<b>Toriyama          Instruments</b>

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.960
Now that I think about it,

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:58.220
Nagomu said he was looking for a senpai 
of his who was supposed to be in Tokyo.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:01.120
But he never found him.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:07.990
I wonder if maybe he was sort of 
waiting for an opportunity to quit.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:12.990
But I really love Nagomu-san's 
guitar playing.

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:15.960
What a coincidence. So do I.

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:18.060
We're just the same.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.620
Itsuka-chan, what's wrong?

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.620
Oh, it's nothing.

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:28.130
There's a jinja over there.

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:29.370
You're right!

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:32.340
Jinja and Buddhist temples really are 
everywhere in Kyoto, aren't they?

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:42.400
Two bows, two claps, 
then one bow. Is that right?

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:43.300
Yes.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.060
Oh, omikuji!

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:55.280
Should we go pull some?

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.040
<b>Omikuji</b>

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.040
<b>Number Thirteen</b>

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.040
<b>Bad Luck</b>

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.040
<b></b>○ Desires: If you do not lose hope,
they will be granted.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:02.040
<b>Omikuji</b>

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:02.040
<b>Number Four</b>

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:02.040
<b>Bad Luck</b>

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:02.040
<b></b>○ Desires: Granting will be 
difficult with little benefit, 
but great ambitions will 
be realized.

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:06.540
<i>"Person you await: Will not come."</i>

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:08.840
Shall we go tie these off?

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.260
Shall we?

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:12.900
What about yours, Itsuka-chan?

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.710
Oh, you got "minor luck." That's not bad!

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:19.060
<b>Omikuji</b>

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:19.060
<b>Number Fifty-Six</b>

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:19.060
<b>Minor Luck</b>

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:19.060
<b></b>\h\h○ Desires: Don't rush.
\h Wait for a good opportunity.

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:19.060
"Person you await..."

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.560
"Running a little late."

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:24.480
Will you take it with you?

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:27.720
Or do you want to tie it off and 
ask the gods to take care of it?

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:30.550
I'll tie it here.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:33.320
I know!

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:36.570
Let's go pull some omikuji 
at a different jinja!

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:38.830
Are we allowed to do that?

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:41.190
We'll entrust these ones to the deities here.

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:45.430
Is there somewhere that seems interesting...

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:48.220
This place might be good!

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:51.550
<b>Kaso Jinja</b>

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:51.550
<b>Deities Enshrined</b>

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:51.550
<b>[Tajimamori no Mikoto]       [Hayashijouin no Mikoto]</b>

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:51.550
<b>Two deities are enshrined: Tajimamori no Mikoto, who brought back the
tachibana orange and became the founder of confections, and Hayashijouin
 no Mikoto, who is said to have been the first in Japan to make manju.</b>

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:51.550
<b>Yoshida Jinja > Kaso Jinja</b>

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:51.550
It's a shrine on the grounds of 
Yoshida Jinja called Kaso Jinja.

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:55.050
A long time ago, by the emperor's command,

00:08:55.050 --> 00:09:00.940
Tajimamori no Mikoto was sent on a journey 
seeking the Tokijiku no Kagu Fruit.

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:06.190
<b>Kaso Jinja</b>

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:06.200
He was was enshrined as a god of sweets at 
the Nakashima Jinja in Hyogo Prefecture,

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:09.510
and Kaso Jinja is a branch of that shrine.

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:14.030
Oh! There are so many names 
of confectionery shops here!

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:23.080
Now that I think about it, I wonder 
what the Tokijiku no Kagu Fruit was.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:27.580
Um... It seems it was a miraculous 
medicine that granted immortality.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:31.480
And now they're known as 
"tachibana," or mikan oranges.

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:34.380
Wow! Starting this year, 
I'm going to eat tons of them!

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:39.040
Both of you, is this your
 first trip to Kaso Jinja?

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:41.700
I've been to other parts of 
Yoshida Jinja a bunch of times.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:45.020
In February, they hold a festival for Setsubun.

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:49.270
When I was little, I went to the 
Setsubun Festival here... just once.

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:57.530
The only memory I have of it 
is the oni making me cry a lot.

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:01.780
Th-That would be traumatic.

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:04.290
But it's fun, too, you know?

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:08.540
There are stalls set up from here all 
the way down to the bottom of the hill.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:13.080
And it can stand up to Kyoto's three biggest 
festivals for how crowded and lively it is!

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:15.020
Really? I'd like to see that!

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:18.300
Then, let's go next year! We'll arrange 
our schedules and all go together!

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:21.920
In that case, shouldn't you
 invite Nagomu first?

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:23.430
<i>Kanoko-san?</i>

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:27.180
If you take him to a jinja 
for sweets, I'm sure he'd love it!

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:31.940
No, for this kind of thing, laughing and 
having fun with just us girls is better, right?

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:34.690
And I want to become better 
friends with you, Kanoko-san.

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:37.560
I feel the same!

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:40.990
<b>Friendship</b>

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:39.350
Mitsuru-chan!

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:45.610
<i>I was stressing out about 
how things would go,</i>

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:47.500
<i>but it looks like I didn't need to worry.</i>

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:50.360
<i>The way they can get along in spite of</i>

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:53.000
<i>whatever else they might 
be thinking is so nice.</i>

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:58.300
<i>Gods, I hope that one day...</i>

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:03.210
<i>I can become as wonderful an adult 
as Mitsuru-chan and Kanoko-san.</i>

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:10.270
Oh! I'll go check the bus schedule.

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:13.320
What is it, Itsuka-chan?

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:16.620
I was just thinking that I'm glad 
it looks like you're having fun.

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:19.740
I thought you might be 
worrying over Kanoko-san.

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:22.750
Oh, you mean her relationship 
with Nagomu-san?

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:25.070
She said they've already broken up.

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:26.480
Instead of being resentful toward her,

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:30.040
being friends will make Nagomu-san 
feel better later, right?

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:31.340
<i>What?</i>

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.040
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:34.030
How did it look?

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:35.930
It said the bus will come in 20 minutes.

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:38.800
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:40.700
Hello, Mom?

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:43.370
What is it, Itsuka-chan?

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:44.800
Nothing, it's just...

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:49.500
I feel like you're being considerate 
of Mitsuru-chan's feelings.

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:53.550
Oh, yes, she does seem to like Nagomu.

00:11:53.550 --> 00:11:55.930
But, well, she's only a 
high schooler, after all.

00:11:55.930 --> 00:11:58.570
Going along with someone who's of an age 
to be in love with the idea of love...

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:00.070
Nagomu's got no time for that sort of thing.

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.200
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:04.520
Is everything all right?

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:07.740
Yes. I was asked to pick up 
ingredients for dinner tonight.

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:12.120
Oh, I have to buy some things too. 
I need to bring back my bento-making.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:15.440
I know! We should exchange bento sometime!

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:17.660
Sounds good! Let's do it!

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:22.300
What is it, Itsuka-chan?

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:27.740
<i>It's scary!</i>

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:34.730
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:34.730
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:33.150
I'm back.

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:34.730
Welcome home!

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:36.780
What? You're giving these to me?

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:39.390
Huh? "Medicine for eternal life?"

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:40.730
Are you telling me to live long?

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:47.030
<b>House Mikan</b>

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:47.030
<b>Medicine for
Eternal Life!!</b>

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:43.140
Why won't you meet my eyes?

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:45.830
Hey! Itsuka?

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:57.770
<i>Nagomu. Nagomu!</i>

00:12:58.440 --> 00:13:02.460
How long are you going to sleep? 
If you don't wake up soon...

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:16.150
Seven o'clock.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:21.830
I have the day off today. 
I'll sleep a little longer.

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:25.240
<i>I dreamed about Grandpa.</i>

00:13:25.550 --> 00:13:27.740
<i>It's almost time for Obon.</i>

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:31.620
<i>When will the Buddhist 
priest be coming by again?</i>

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:34.540
It's today!

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:37.000
<b>We are
closed
 today.</b>

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.750
This is the zabuton for the priest, right?

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:42.410
That's right. That spot is good.

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:48.260
What's this? Did you wake 
up and come down in a panic?

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:49.450
Of course not.

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:52.160
My mornings begin with contemplation.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:53.920
Today, I took our Obon 
service into account and—

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:55.770
I'm amazed you can say that,
 dressed as you are.

00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:59.110
<i>Why is this person popular with women?</i>

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:03.560
Coming!

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:05.030
He's here.

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:08.030
Then I shall begin.

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:16.790
<i>It's been ten years since 
I last saw this scene.</i>

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:20.290
<b>I
N
 
M
E
M
O
R
I
A
M
 
K
O
U
T
O
K
U</b>

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:20.290
<i>I wonder if Grandpa has already 
come back here by now.</i>

00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:24.710
<i>Huh? Isn't there someone 
missing from this gathering?</i>

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:29.550
Oh, my.

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:32.300
I didn't make it in time again.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:33.310
G...

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:34.810
Grandma?!

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.560
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.560
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:39.560
I'm sorry. I was late for the bus.

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:44.070
Here, presents. I chose things 
I thought you'd like, so don't complain.

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:46.570
Oh, what a lovely obi brooch.

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:48.820
Oh, it's so cute!

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.820
<b>Wakame</b>

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.820
<b>From Sanriku</b>

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.820
<b>It expands</b>

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.820
<b>Hair Growth</b>

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.820
<b>Absolutely
 Effective</b>

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:53.830
Mother, this year, I will say it.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:57.830
<b>I'm in Okinawa! It's really hot here.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:57.830
Why do you only come home once a year?!

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.450
After Father passed away,

00:14:59.450 --> 00:15:02.200
you've traveled all over, having fun,
 for how many years now?

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:05.210
You kept all my postcards 
so nicely! That's adorable.

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:07.840
I'm going to ask a temple 
to purify them with fire!

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:11.800
What's it hurt? This place has 
been entrusted to you, after all.

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:13.440
I'm done with work and raising children,

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:15.970
so now I'm getting my fill of 
all the things I've wanted to do.

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:19.120
And it's easier on Fuki-san because she 
doesn't have to be conscientious towards me.

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:21.310
Not at all! I'm still 
nowhere near good enough.

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:22.680
Itsuka-chan...

00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:23.520
Y-Yes?

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:27.360
I hear you're working hard in 
the shop and at your studies.

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:29.750
That's commendable of you.

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:32.110
Thank you.

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:33.310
And...

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:34.990
Who were you again?

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:37.310
I'm your grandson, Nagomu!

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:38.370
I know that.

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.370
<b>Oedo
 Banana</b>

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.370
Here's your present.

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:42.120
<b>I
N
 
M
E
M
O
R
I
A
M
 
K
O
U
T
O
K
U</b>

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:03.400
This is the moment when your 
father is most anxious.

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:07.980
The one who knows Ryokushou's flavors 
best is his mother, after all.

00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:13.750
Whenever she comes back, he asks 
her to check the an like that.

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:17.030
Yes, that's fine.

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:21.640
The an is the cornerstone 
of everything for us.

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:26.280
Taking care of Ryokushou's 
flavors is your job now.

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:27.540
I know that.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:28.840
Please do well.

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:31.690
Dad...

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:37.500
I can't tell if he's angry with 
Grandma or if he really trusts her.

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:39.060
What are you talking about?

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:41.920
That's just what relationships are like.

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:43.620
It's fine if you don't understand.

00:16:44.470 --> 00:16:46.650
Work hard at your training.

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:50.120
Starting tomorrow, your grandmother
 will be instructing you.

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:51.720
Huh?

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:57.700
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:57.700
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:57.050
Ow!

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:01.400
With that poor posture and lack of nerve, 
do you really think you can move snappily?

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:02.120
Yes, ma'am!

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:04.870
<b>Don't forget to
wash your hands
and gargle!</b>

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:03.900
There are too many dirty dishes!

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:04.870
Yes, ma'am!

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:07.370
Don't spill the flour!

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:09.500
I'll spill even more if you do that!

00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:12.760
You have to take action after 
thinking two or three steps ahead.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:15.510
If you wait for direction, 
you'll never improve!

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:15.510
Yes, ma'am!

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:24.270
That Zen striking stick... 
I didn't know she still used it.

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:28.880
Letting your summer homework 
pile up like this...

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:32.110
If you don't start anticipating two or 
three steps ahead, what will you do?

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:34.030
Yes, ma'am!

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:38.440
<i>This year's Obon... Am I gonna
 live to see the end of it?</i>

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:42.320
Are you worried?

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:44.040
N-No, it's nothing like that!

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:49.340
Hey! Once you've used a tool, 
put it back where you found it!

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:51.850
Yes, ma'am!

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:59.600
<i>When I met her, she was always so shy.</i>

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:02.200
<i>Once she started helping me with work,</i>

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:04.650
<i>she'd steel herself and work fiercely.</i>

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:07.950
The cuteness of the grandson 
she hasn't seen for ten years

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:10.400
is probably making her even more fired up.

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:14.410
Well, it's only for a little while. 
Keep at it with her, won't you?

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:18.280
<i>I had another dream about Grandpa.</i>

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:24.540
<i>I guess I might as well wake up.</i>

00:18:33.730 --> 00:18:35.050
Kazuteru-san,

00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:40.120
watch over everyone's work 
again today, won't you?

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:44.840
<i>Maybe I'll dawdle just a little longer.</i>

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:49.520
You overslept!

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:51.530
I'm sorry!

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:52.310
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:52.310
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:56.540
Well, thank you for coming!

00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:58.820
It's Obon, so I came to do some sightseeing!

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:02.400
You have such a nice shop here.

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:00.600
Who are they?

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:02.820
She said she met them 
while she was traveling.

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:04.910
Oh, thank you so much!

00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:05.290
A lot of others have come, too.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:08.540
They stop by, saying that they've 
heard about this place from her.

00:19:08.430 --> 00:19:11.320
Itsuka-chan, you look very cute.

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:09.560
Wow.

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:13.840
She says she just wanders 
around wherever she wants,

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:17.340
Yes, she does look adorable. 
And such a good worker.

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:17.340
but she's always thinking of us and the shop.

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:18.090
Isn't she?

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:20.100
Really...

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:25.350
Tomorrow is the 16th, isn't it?

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:29.040
Itsuka-chan, Nagomu! Tomorrow, 
let's go write our gomagi sticks.

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:31.640
We'll leave at six in the morning.

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:41.400
<b>Philosopher's Path</b>

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:41.400
It's so nice and cool at 
this time of day, isn't it?

00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:44.030
Do we just keep going up this way?

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:46.720
Yes, straight that way is Ginkakuji.

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:49.130
Behind it is the mountain 
where they set Daimonji.

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:53.820
This is the first time I've written gomagi.

00:19:53.820 --> 00:19:55.080
What? Is it?

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:59.420
The first time I went was 
with your grandfather.

00:20:00.580 --> 00:20:05.340
We'd just started Ryokushou, 
and we were so busy.

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:09.320
We went around introducing the shop, 
so that people would remember the name.

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:12.070
And we often went to entreat the gods, too.

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:14.810
These gomagi were one 
of the ways we did that.

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:17.820
<b>Prosperous
Business</b>

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:17.820
<b>Prosperous
 Business</b>

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:17.820
Both of us wrote "prosperous business" on them.

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:21.510
We laughed so hard, saying, 
"You wrote the same thing!"

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:27.180
So the gomagi will be burned up the 
mountain where the kanji is written?

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:28.330
<b>Dai</b>

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:28.330
That's right.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:31.280
And then our ancestors who 
have come to visit us

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:33.950
will go back with them into the sky.

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:35.870
So, have you both written yours?

00:20:35.870 --> 00:20:36.650
Yes.

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:39.380
<b>Earnest
Wishes
 Realized</b>

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:39.640
Nagomu has, "improving 
artistic accomplishments."

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:43.090
<b>\h\h\hImproving
\hArtistic
Accomplishments</b>

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:43.090
<b>Earnest
Wishes
 Realized</b>

00:20:39.640 --> 00:20:41.800
And Itsuka-chan has, 
"earnest wishes realized."

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:43.090
Very nice!

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:46.090
Grandma, did you write 
"prosperous business" again?

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:47.850
No, I wrote...

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:49.140
this.

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:49.850
<b>Long Life and
 Good Fortune</b>

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:51.210
Huh? Long life?

00:20:51.210 --> 00:20:52.850
Why are you so surprised?

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:55.980
No, I just thought you'd ask 
for something about the shop.

00:20:55.980 --> 00:21:00.610
I've already done that more than enough. 
I'm sure the Buddha is sick of hearing it.

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:03.110
There are still places 
I want to go, after all.

00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:04.860
And...

00:21:05.470 --> 00:21:11.320
I have to watch you become a 
full-fledged artisan in his place.

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:23.020
Is something wrong?

00:21:23.020 --> 00:21:25.630
No, it's nothing.

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:29.640
<b>Dai</b>

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:29.640
<b>KYOTO'S FIVE MOUNTAIN SEND-OFF FIRES</b>

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:32.940
Yes, leisurely watching it
from home is the best.

00:21:32.940 --> 00:21:35.590
You can see all the mountains this way.

00:21:37.320 --> 00:21:40.330
Mother, please have some kuzu manju.

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:42.310
We're having them in place of send-off dango.

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:44.110
Thank you.

00:21:49.430 --> 00:21:50.120
Yes.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:55.120
<b>Dai</b>

00:21:51.700 --> 00:21:53.460
The flavor is perfect.

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:33.970
A postcard from Mother has arrived.

00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:38.040
Apparently, she's in Tohoku right now,
 helping with a friend's shop.

00:23:38.040 --> 00:23:41.130
So that's how she makes her money.

00:23:41.130 --> 00:23:44.360
<i>P.S. I'm not as good with 
the striking stick as I was.</i>

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:46.980
<i>I'll train at a temple before I come back.</i>

00:23:46.980 --> 00:23:49.990
Grandma! You don't have to do that anymore!

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:52.320
It's the district sports festival.

00:23:49.990 --> 00:24:10.010
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:49.990 --> 00:24:10.010
<b>"Autumn's Potato Moon"</b>

00:23:52.940 --> 00:23:56.200
This year, everyone in the 
family will participate again!

00:24:00.790 --> 00:24:03.540
I've come to collect Itsuka.

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:05.840
She doesn't rely on anyone.

00:24:06.500 --> 00:24:10.010
Please make Itsuka into someone 
who depends on others.
